<title>RUSSIA: Russian current a/c surplus narrows in Q2.</title>
<headline>Russian current a/c surplus narrows in Q2.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's surplus on the current account balance of payments narrowed to $2.84 billion in the second quarter from $4.45 billion in the first quarter, the Central Bank said in its latest bulletin.</p>
<p>The central bank issued the following balance of payments data (figures in millions of dollars).</p>
<p>    EXCLUDING FORMER SOVIET UNION Q2 1996    Q1 1996    Q2 1996</p>
<p>    Current account balance	  +2,839     +4,445	  n/a</p>
<p>    Merchandise trade		  +5,902     +5,132	  n/a</p>
<p>	  Exports (FOB)		 +16,818    +15,131	  n/a</p>
<p>	  Imports (FOB)		 -10,916     -9,999	  n/a</p>
<p>    Direct investment balance	   +73	 +401	  n/a</p>
<p>	 Investment in Russia	    +235	 +430	  n/a</p>
<p>    Portfolio investment balance     +832     +1,192	  n/a</p>
<p>    New government borrowing net     +899     +2,779	  n/a</p>
<p>    WITH ALL COUNTRIES		Q2 1996    Q1 1996    Q2 1995</p>
<p>    Current account balance	  +2,293     +4,682	  n/a</p>
<p>    Merchandise trade		  +5,392     +5,321	  n/a</p>
<p>	  Exports (FOB)		 +21,017    +19,958	  n/a</p>
<p>	  Imports (FOB)		 -15,625    -14,637	  n/a</p>
<p>    WITH ALL COUNTRIES		     H1 1996     H1 1995</p>
<p>    Current account balance		 +6,975	+9,001</p>
<p>    Merchandise trade			+10,712     +12,403</p>
<p>	  Exports (FOB)			+40,974     +38,925</p>
<p>	  Imports (FOB)			-30,262     -26,522</p>
<p>    Direct investment balance		 +483	  +280</p>
<p>	 Investment in Russia		   +686	  +472</p>
<p>    Portfolio investment balance	  +2,023	-1,497</p>
<p>NOTES - Government borrowing figures show hard currency</p>
<p>only.</p>
<p>--Jonathan Lynn, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
